id: bible-in-a-year
title: The Bible in a year
version: 1
creator: Day by Word
summary: The 66 books of the Protestant canon, Genesis to Revelation, in
  the order they are printed, in 365 readings of whole chapters balanced by
  reading time.
suits: Readers who want to read every book in order and can give about ten
  minutes on most days, and up to fifteen for the longest readings.
schedule: sequence
behaviors: pace, finish-date
reading-days: 7
coverage: whole-bible
canon: protestant
books: all
limitations: It reads the 66 books only; the deuterocanonical books (also
  called the Apocrypha), which Catholic and Orthodox Bibles include, are
  not in it. It reads in printed order, not the order of events, and the
  New Testament begins at reading 281. It has no rest days of its own; read
  five days a week, it takes 73 weeks.
instructions: Read the next reading whenever you read, in any Bible. To
  finish in a year, read one reading a day, or choose a finish date and
  Day by Word will show what each reading day asks. If you miss a day, your
  next reading waits for you.
source: An original plan by Day by Word. The Old Testament and the New are
  each divided into readings of whole chapters, as even in reading time as
  whole chapters allow; some readings run from the end of one book into the
  next. Reading times are estimated from word counts of the World English
  Bible, a public-domain translation; the plan can be read in any
  translation.
rights: daybyword-original
review: reviewed
